# Compatibility pass for Compact Work Tab.
#
# Direct inspection of its 1.6 assembly settled the earlier question: it patches the existing
# PawnColumnWorker_WorkPriority headers/cells and recalculates its layout from table.Columns.
# It does not own or restore a competing column list, and its own README explicitly supports mods
# that add work types. About.xml therefore no longer declares it incompatible. Keep this map as
# the optional coexistence pass and replay it when Compact Work Tab changes.
#
# packageId read from the installed copy's own About.xml, 2026-09-21.
#
# Not in this set, and not a gap in About.xml either: CaptainArbitrary.CompactWorkTab (Workshop
# 3027381000), the original this one continues. It carries a DIFFERENT packageId, so
# <incompatibleWith> does not name it - but its own About.xml lists supportedVersions 1.4 only and
# ships a 1.4/ folder, so it does not run in 1.6. Read from the installed copy, 2026-09-21. This
# file said the opposite for a few hours, on the strength of the packageId alone; nobody running
# 1.6 has it active, and no set is worth a run to prove a mod that never loads.
#
# packageId             workshopId   what it is
Mlie.CompactWorkTab     3250322299   Compact Work Tab (Continued), optional coexistence target
#
# The steps scenario 2 clicks with, staged in every pass so the scenarios do not change between them.
nelim.pickletools.clickdiagnostics   path:PickleTools/ClickDiagnostics/Mod
